# Project summary and structure

The goal of this project is to make declaration data easy to search, browse and interpret.

- `exposed/` contains the rust application and CLI code that powers the project.
- `frontend/` contains a simple Svelte application
- `ingest/` contains the legacy Python scripts used to bootstrap this project.

## Exposed coding policy

- Follow with strict detail to the existing style of the application. This includes:
  - Type driven design
  - Domain modelling and parse-not-validate
  - Consistent error handling
  - Service layer abstractions

- Interactions with the database must use `sqlx` macros for compile-time query verification.

- For Rust changes, read and apply the
  [Rust domain development skill](.agents/skills/rust-domain-development/SKILL.md).
- Before implementation, identify the domain states, invariants, and the type
  that owns each rule. Parse external values into those types at boundaries and
  retain typed values internally.
- Use one canonical domain enum for each finite vocabulary. Do not duplicate
  its variants in string allowlists. Use exhaustive matches where behavior
  depends on a variant.
- When a bug exposes duplicated domain rules, remove the duplication rather
  than synchronizing the copies. Trace changes through producers, serialization,
  consumers, and persistence together.

## Frontend coding policy

- The frontend is largely in a prototype stage so changes can be made freely without much guidance.
- Every PR that changes the UI must include desktop screenshots in its
  description. Capture the affected views from the running application on
  the PR branch after completing the changes.
- Upload screenshots as GitHub attachments with `gh pr create --attach` or
  `gh pr edit --attach`. Use a GitHub CLI version that supports this flag. Never
  commit PR screenshots to the repository. Verify that the attachments render
  in the PR description before marking the PR ready for review.


## Ingest coding policy

- When porting code from this project, do not replicate the style. Use it as an end to end guide for functionality.

## Worktree policy

- For read-only tasks (investigating, reading, summarizing, or describing code),
  work on the current branch without creating a worktree.
- For tasks that require changing code or other files, work in a dedicated Git
  worktree before making changes. If a read-only task expands to require changes,
  switch to a dedicated worktree first.
- For such changes, reuse this chat's dedicated worktree if one already exists.
  Otherwise, create a sibling worktree with a unique branch and perform all
  edits, installs, and checks there.
- Never modify the primary checkout.
- Report the worktree path and branch when starting work in a dedicated worktree.

## Git history

- After completing and validating a task, commit its changes on the task's work
  branch without waiting for a separate request.
- Never commit directly on `main`.
- Keep Git history linear. Rebase feature branches onto the target branch and
  integrate changes with a fast-forward or squash; do not create merge commits.

## Development database migrations

- Keep schema changes in `db/migrations` as SQLx versioned `.up.sql` and
  `.down.sql` pairs. From the repository root, create a pair with
  `sqlx migrate add --source db/migrations --reversible <name>`.
- Never change a migration file that existed before the current PR. Treat those
  migrations as immutable, even when they have not been applied locally.
- When a PR's schema design changes, you must edit, consolidate, or remove the
  migrations introduced by that PR. Do not append a corrective migration for an
  obsolete step in the same PR. Before review, the PR must contain only the
  migrations needed for its final schema. Recreate isolated test databases that
  applied a discarded PR migration; do not preserve obsolete steps just to
  satisfy their checksums.
- Do not fold changes into the baseline or put manual schema scripts in
  `db/upgrades`.
- From the repository root, apply migrations with
  `sqlx migrate run --config sqlx.toml --source db/migrations`, inspect them with
  `sqlx migrate info --config sqlx.toml --source db/migrations`, and revert the
  latest version with
  `sqlx migrate revert --config sqlx.toml --source db/migrations`.
  Commands read the root `.env`; set `DATABASE_URL` to select another database.
- SQLx owns each migration transaction. Do not add `BEGIN` or `COMMIT` to the
  migration files. Keep each down migration limited to its up migration's changes.
- Test forward upgrades with existing records and the full down/up cycle in an
  isolated database. Preserve imported data when upgrading an existing database.
- The one-time transition from the consolidated baseline requires schema and
  data verification before aligning its checksum. Follow `db/README.md`;
  changing the checksum alone does not apply schema changes.
//! CLI inbound port

use schemars::JsonSchema;
use std::{path::PathBuf, str::FromStr};

use clap::{Parser, Subcommand};
use serde::Serialize;

use crate::{
    domain::{
        models::declaration_loading::DeclarationLoadOutcome,
        models::entity_ingestion::{
            DeclarationIngestionStage, EntityIngestionRequest, IngestionKey, MemberIngestionStage,
        },
        services::declaration_cleaning::DeclarationCleanerService,
        services::declaration_fetch::DeclarationFetcherService,
        services::declaration_loading::DeclarationLoaderService,
        services::declaration_resolution::DeclarationResolverService,
        services::entity_ingestion::{
            EntityFetcherService, EntityIngesterService, FetcherService, IngesterService,
        },
    },
    inbound::cli::config::{
        DataConfig, DeclarationFetcherConfig, DeclarationResolverConfig, FetcherConfig,
        LoaderConfig,
    },
    outbound::{ExposedDataPipeline, ExposedDatabase, ParliamentApiClient, WeldrsFunderScorer},
};

pub mod config;
mod migrate;
pub mod response;
mod response_help;

pub use migrate::{MigrateArgs, run_migrate};
pub use response::{CliSuccess, IntoResponse, Response};

/// CLI entrypoint for the `exposed` project
#[derive(Parser)]
pub struct ExposedCli {
    /// Commands for CLI
    #[command(subcommand)]
    pub command: Commands,
}

/// Run a server, prepare application data, or apply database migrations
#[derive(Subcommand)]
pub enum Commands {
    /// Start an instance of the `exposed` server
    Server,
    /// Options to run the `exposed` data pipeline
    Data(DataArgs),
    /// Apply database migrations explicitly.
    Migrate(MigrateArgs),
}

/// CLI Data Args
#[derive(Parser)]
pub struct DataArgs {
    #[command(subcommand)]
    command: DataCommands,
}

/// CLI Subcommands
#[derive(Subcommand)]
#[allow(missing_docs)]
pub enum DataCommands {
    /// Show the latest ingestion key and directory path.
    #[command(after_long_help = response_help::single(latest))]
    Latest {
        /// YAML configuration with the ingestion `data_dir`.
        #[arg(long)]
        config: PathBuf,
    },
    /// Copy the latest raw capture into a new ingestion run.
    #[command(after_long_help = response_help::single(copy_latest_raw))]
    CopyLatestRaw {
        /// YAML configuration with the ingestion `data_dir`.
        #[arg(long)]
        config: PathBuf,
        /// Destination ingestion key. Defaults to a fresh UUID-v7.
        #[arg(long)]
        ingestion_key: Option<IngestionKey>,
    },
    #[command(after_long_help = response_help::declarations())]
    Declarations {
        /// Stage to run: fetch, clean, resolve, or load.
        #[arg(value_parser = ["fetch", "clean", "resolve", "load"])]
        stage: String,
        /// YAML configuration containing the declaration `data_dir`.
        #[arg(long)]
        config: PathBuf,
        /// Ingestion run to clean, resolve, or load.
        #[arg(long)]
        ingestion_key: Option<IngestionKey>,
    },
    #[command(after_long_help = response_help::single(members))]
    Members {
        stage: String,
        #[arg(long)]
        config: PathBuf,
        #[arg(long)]
        ingestion_key: Option<IngestionKey>,
    },
}

/// Entry point for CLI commands
///
/// Command failures remain in the response until [`Response::write_to`] is called.
///
/// Failures include:
/// - Bad stage arg
/// - Bad config path
/// - Bad config shape
/// - Missing or non-Unicode `DATABASE_URL` for commands that use the database
/// - Service level failures
pub async fn run_cli(args: DataArgs) -> Response {
    match args.command {
        DataCommands::Latest { config } => latest(config).await.into_response(),
        DataCommands::CopyLatestRaw {
            config,
            ingestion_key,
        } => copy_latest_raw(config, ingestion_key).await.into_response(),
        DataCommands::Declarations {
            stage,
            config,
            ingestion_key,
        } => declarations(stage, config, ingestion_key).await,
        DataCommands::Members {
            stage,
            config,
            ingestion_key,
        } => members(stage, config, ingestion_key).await.into_response(),
    }
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct IngestionResponse<T> {
    /// Ingestion result, or null when the store has no source runs.
    ingestion: Option<T>,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct IngestionLocation {
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    /// Absolute ingestion run directory.
    path: PathBuf,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct CopiedIngestion {
    /// Run whose raw capture was copied.
    source_ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    /// Absolute destination ingestion run directory.
    path: PathBuf,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct StageAcknowledgement<S> {
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    stage: S,
    /// Absolute raw artifact: raw/declarations directory or raw/members.parquet file.
    path: PathBuf,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct DeclarationCleaningResponse {
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    /// Absolute cleaned/declarations artifact directory.
    path: PathBuf,
    /// Raw member partitions, including empty partitions.
    member_partitions: usize,
    /// Declarations, including those with no funding.
    declarations: usize,
    /// Original funding occurrences.
    funding_entries: usize,
    /// Source-role funder observations across declaration and funding scopes.
    funders: usize,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct DeclarationResolutionResponse {
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    /// Absolute resolved/declarations artifact directory.
    path: PathBuf,
    /// Source funder observations, including unresolved names.
    observations: usize,
    /// Original funding occurrences, counted once.
    payments: usize,
    /// Retained pair decisions between funder observations.
    pairs: usize,
}

#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
struct DeclarationLoadingResponse {
    ingestion_key: IngestionKey,
    /// Whether this call imported the run or confirmed an exact retry.
    outcome: DeclarationLoadOutcome,
    declarations: usize,
    /// Distinct resolved identities referenced by selected attributions.
    funders: usize,
    /// Original funding occurrences, including unavailable attributions.
    funding_entries: usize,
}

async fn latest(
    config: PathBuf,
) -> anyhow::Result<CliSuccess<IngestionResponse<IngestionLocation>>> {
    let config = LoaderConfig::try_from(&config)?;
    let ingestion = ExposedDataPipeline::latest_ingestion(&config.data_dir)
        .await?
        .map(|(path, ingestion_key)| IngestionLocation {
            ingestion_key,
            path,
        });
    Ok(CliSuccess::new(IngestionResponse { ingestion }))
}

async fn copy_latest_raw(
    config: PathBuf,
    ingestion_key: Option<IngestionKey>,
) -> anyhow::Result<CliSuccess<IngestionResponse<CopiedIngestion>>> {
    let config = LoaderConfig::try_from(&config)?;
    let ingestion_key = ingestion_key.unwrap_or_default();
    let ingestion = ExposedDataPipeline::copy_latest_raw(&config.data_dir, ingestion_key.clone())
        .await?
        .map(|(path, source_ingestion_key)| CopiedIngestion {
            source_ingestion_key,
            ingestion_key,
            path,
        });
    Ok(CliSuccess::new(IngestionResponse { ingestion }))
}

async fn declarations(
    stage: String,
    config: PathBuf,
    ingestion_key: Option<IngestionKey>,
) -> Response {
    let stage = match DeclarationIngestionStage::from_str(&stage) {
        Ok(stage) => stage,
        Err(error) => return Err::<Response, _>(error).into_response(),
    };
    match stage {
        DeclarationIngestionStage::Fetch => fetch_declarations(config, ingestion_key)
            .await
            .into_response(),
        DeclarationIngestionStage::Clean => clean_declarations(config, ingestion_key)
            .await
            .into_response(),
        DeclarationIngestionStage::Resolve => resolve_declarations(config, ingestion_key)
            .await
            .into_response(),
        DeclarationIngestionStage::Load => load_declarations(config, ingestion_key)
            .await
            .into_response(),
    }
}

use clap::Parser;
use exposed::inbound::{
    cli::{Commands, ExposedCli, IntoResponse, Response, run_cli, run_migrate},
    http::server::run_server,
};

fn main() -> anyhow::Result<std::process::ExitCode> {
    let args = ExposedCli::parse();
    match args.command {
        Commands::Server => run_server().map(|()| std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS),
        Commands::Migrate(args) => {
            dotenvy::dotenv().ok();
            let response = match tokio::runtime::Runtime::new() {
                Ok(runtime) => runtime.block_on(run_migrate(args)),
                Err(error) => Err::<Response, _>(error).into_response(),
            };
            Ok(response.write_to(std::io::stdout().lock(), std::io::stderr().lock())?)
        }
        Commands::Data(args) => {
            dotenvy::dotenv().ok();
            let response = match tokio::runtime::Runtime::new() {
                Ok(runtime) => runtime.block_on(run_cli(args)),
                Err(error) => Err::<Response, _>(error).into_response(),
            };
            Ok(response.write_to(std::io::stdout().lock(), std::io::stderr().lock())?)
        }
    }
}

